nd then two  days later he took it back saying that  he didn't have the courage so why does  this question bring up such strong  feelings within the industry if he  aauggh a hero who's kind of mythical  than you know everyone can kind of  project whatever they want on to him  whereas if it turns into a like a real  living breathing figure then all of a  sudden it's it's a person and you can go  and criticize this tax history in a sex  life and it's a really different story  satoshis mysterious identity helped  Bitcoin attract such an ideologically  diverse following by allowing its  devotees to attach their own meanings to  this hard-to-define  technology but most people agree that  today it's taken on a life of its own  everyone understands that it is detached  from any single person the incentives  built in the system are really beautiful  and so a lots of people have an  incentive to make it work  it's gratifying to see events like this  it shows if you have a great technology  and you make an open and available to  the world the world will eventually  notice it might take a few years but  people will notice  you
 

